Title: "Open Text"
Id: "08d20959-2312-4919-8756-01832cdc416d"

Text: "`OpenText` is quoted prose text.

```mlg-fragment
Text: \"A paragraph of Markdown prose.\"
```

The structural parser removes the enclosing quotes. Ordinary quoted text
decodes escaped double quotes while preserving other backslashes. Triple-quoted
text preserves its contents literally and can contain unescaped double quotes.

`OpenText` is used by prose blocks, theorem titles, biographies, resource fields, descriptions, and many metadata fields. In viewer prose contexts, Markdown and LaTeX are rendered.

Because open text is prose, command-looking text inside it is not treated as a semantic command reference unless another feature explicitly parses it. Open text may embed inline `&#123;. ... .&#125;` or display `&#123;&#123;. ... .&#125;&#125;` formulations, as well as `&#123;: ... :&#125;` theorem references."
Id: "9d32e6e1-328b-48af-9abe-9bf27cdfa7bf"
